{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the parabola parametrized by $r(t)=2t\\,i+(2-{t}^{2})\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2t,\\,y(t)=2-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2\\,i-2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}]dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+2-{t}^{2})\\cdot 2+2t\\cdot (-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{t}^{2}+4t+4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+4t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-2+2+4)-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78cf788dcf95d0df111c1b5b515c5b41bebdf8fea6d7e50ee118558903618f6b"} {"question" "q-124670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{12}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-z\\,dy+y\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=3{t}^{2}\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=3{t}^{2},\\,y(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3{t}^{2}\\cdot (6t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9{cos}^{2}⁡t-9{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9\\,dt \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{t}^{4}}{2}-9t){|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78cf788dcf95d0df111c1b5b515c5b41bebdf8fea6d7e50ee118558903618f6b"} {"question" "q-124712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13{\\pi }^{2}+5"] ["math" "24{\\pi }^{4}"] ["math" "36{\\pi }^{4}"] ["math" "60{\\pi }^{2}-12\\pi "] ["math" "72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+{z}^{2}\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+{z}^{2}\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+{z}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}(-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+{z}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+{t}^{4}\\cdot (2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4{sin}^{2}⁡t-4{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78cf788dcf95d0df111c1b5b515c5b41bebdf8fea6d7e50ee118558903618f6b"} {"question" "q-124830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}+2\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{3}+{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{4}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{4}-2{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2{t}^{5}-4\\,dt"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124874" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+y\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+{t}^{3}\\,k$ for $t\\in [3,5]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124874" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)={t}^{2},\\,z(t)={t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+2t\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+y\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}xy\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}(xy\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{t}^{3}\\cdot (1)+{t}^{2}\\cdot (2t)+{t}^{3}\\cdot (3{t}^{2})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}3{t}^{5}+3{t}^{3}\\,dt \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{3}^{5}{t}^{5}+{t}^{3}\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124874" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78cf788dcf95d0df111c1b5b515c5b41bebdf8fea6d7e50ee118558903618f6b"} {"question" "q-124874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{\\int }_{3}^{5}t+5\\,dt"] ["math" "3{\\int }_{3}^{5}{t}^{4}+t\\,dt"] ["math" "3{\\int }_{3}^{5}{t}^{5}+{t}^{3}\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{3}^{5}{t}^{2}+5\\,dt"] ["math" "{\\int }_{3}^{5}{t}^{5}+13t\\,dt"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{\\int }_{3}^{5}{t}^{5}+{t}^{3}\\,dt"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,dx-z\\,dy+{y}^{2}\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [2,6]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)={t}^{2},\\,z(t)={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+2t\\,j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,dx-z\\,dy+{y}^{2}\\,dz & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot (1)-{t}^{2}\\cdot (2t)+{t}^{4}\\cdot (2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2{t}^{5}-2{t}^{3}\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069853/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2b1c0b69ec5d235c9b4fb236851eb76f6c1617c1b99178a0375fcb1cac93d13"} {"question" "q-124879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty